 &lt;div class="container">
 &lt;div class="third-contents">
 &lt;h2>About the portal&lt;/h2>
 &lt;div class="third-contents-inner">
This portal is a part of &lt;a href="https://pathogendatanetwork.org">Pathogen Data Network&lt;/a>,
a global consortium coordinated by the
&lt;a href="https://www.sib.swiss/">SIB (Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics&lt;/a>,
and is operated by &lt;a href="https://www.ddbj.nig.ac.jp">DNA Data Bank of Japan (DDBJ)&lt;/a>.

The website is built using Hugo on GitHub based on the theme of
&lt;a href="https://scilifelab.se/data/">SciLifeLab Data Centre&lt;/a>.
We make all our codes open source under the MIT license. 
 &lt;br/>&lt;br/>
 &lt;/div>
 &lt;h2>History&lt;/h2>
 &lt;div class="third-contents-inner">
An original portal was launched by &lt;a href="https://rcos.nii.ac.jp/">RCOS&lt;/a>
(Research Center for Open Science and Data Platform, National Institute of Informatics)
as "COVID-19 Data Portal Japan" in 2020 in collaboration with other COVID-19 data portals.
The current version started as a DDBJ service in 2025.
 &lt;/div>
 &lt;/div>
